WEBVTT

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:06.760
Once, the world was invaded
by beasts from the world of Disas.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.980
They possessed the power
to neutralize modern science,

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:12.540
and humanity was powerless against them.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.480
But there were those who offered
salvation to humanity in its hour of need.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.080
The Spirit World.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.130
With the help of the Spirit World,

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.920
Magical Girls were born.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:27.460
After a fierce battle,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.420
the Disas were driven from Earth.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.330
Even after the great war ended,

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.800
cooperation continued between
the Spirit World and Earth:

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.390
technology sharing, trade,

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:46.860
and defense cooperation
for when the Disas returned.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.150
It's summer over there.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:57.610
Do you have it?

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.730
Yes, Tabira-sama.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.820
It's right here, ru.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.740
Wait for me...

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:12.640
My beloved Magical Girls.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.020
<b>The Lid of Hell</b>

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:54.020
<b>JGSDF Naha Garrison</b>

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:58.660
So this is why you dragged
us away from our field trip.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:01.920
The 6th Naha Two-World Conference on Trade...

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:04.140
And we're supposed to protect it?

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.420
I'm sorry we didn't tell you earlier.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.360
It's top secret, you see.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.700
"Top secret" doesn't mean you can...

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.430
It's probably a lie!

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:17.170
He's just trying to make
it harder for you to refuse.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:20.880
I knew all about it, chu!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.140
Then why didn't you tell me?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.140
The plan is for <i>her</i> to come
from the Spirit World.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.280
You mean...

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.670
General Tabira?

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.110
Is that why,

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.680
Iizuka-san?

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:38.680
What are you talking about?

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:41.200
<b>Conference Room 2</b>

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:43.860
You guys!

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.020
Hey!

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.580
It's been a while!

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:51.000
It really has!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.930
Well, um...

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.230
After the war ended three years ago,

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:06.380
everybody went to join their home
country's military and stuff.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.130
I know there are all these conflicts,
and our countries want different things,

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.390
so it can't be like it was before, probably.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:16.350
But we all survived that awful war together.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.840
So I'm happy to see you all again.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.030
Asuka-san!

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.220
Asuka...

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:33.130
This time I'm here as part of the 
UN Magical Security Council's observers.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.710
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:39.660
Yeah.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.010
Hey there.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.340
Where are Asuka and Kurumi?

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:51.630
Asuka-san had to go back all of a sudden
'cause of something involving her dad.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:53.810
And Kurumi-san said she'd go, too.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.930
Why Kurumi, too?

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.150
She said she couldn't leave Asuka-san alone.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:09.610
It's so peaceful here, you know.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.050
Yeah.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.230
Maybe 'cause we're closer to the equator.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.580
It feels like the air is different.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.330
I don't want to go home at all.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.620
I know what you mean.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.860
Want to live here?

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.150
We could fish for food and stuff.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:25.810
Fish, huh?

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.720
I'd like some meat too, though.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.040
Um...

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:31.030
Excuse me.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.320
Could you take a photo for us?

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.800
Sure thing.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:37.150
Okay, you two.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.170
You need to get closer or you won't fit.

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.150
Get real close!

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:42.770
Closer!

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.110
Yeah!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.880
Thank you.

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.270
Not a problem!

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:57.210
Nobody really notices anything
wrong with the way you look, huh?

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:00.950
What did we look like to them, I wonder?

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.870
The concealment magic
makes us hard to remember.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.720
They'll probably forget quickly.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.410
I see.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:14.400
They said it was peaceful here, didn't they?

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:16.420
Yeah.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:21.570
What will they think tomorrow, I wonder?

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:31.450
<b>Naha Garrison Barracks</b>

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.120
<b>You scared me when you just
ran off like that. Is your dad okay?</b>

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.120
<b>Roger!</b>

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:46.550
<b>Yeah. It was nothing</b>

00:06:44.290 --> 00:06:48.300
<b>I see. Sorry you had
to leave Okinawa early</b>

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:54.220
<b>Tomorrow's free time
 I'll buy you something in the city and 
bring it back
Let's hang out again when I get home</b>

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.090
Yeah.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.620
It's a promise.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:19.910
<b>Squeeze</b>

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:19.910
Squeeze!

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:23.660
Oh, Asuka was so cute when she cried!

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:26.470
Magical Girl Trivia!

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.830
Tamara loves cute things!

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.260
She needs a gigantic,

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:33.840
fluffy stuffed animal to get
 a good night's sleep, chu!

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:37.080
<i>Asuka is so cute.</i>

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.790
<i>My big sister is the one
who's most important,</i>

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.860
<i>but Asuka's also...</i>

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.610
<b>Naha International Street Shopping District</b>

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:58.470
And thus,

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:01.800
night passed for the Magical Girls, chu.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.260
<b>Distonia Military Expeditionary Strike Brigade
Forward Observation Disas</b>

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:18.350
<b>Expeditionary Strike Brigade
Fire Control Disas</b>

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:20.090
We're looking good.

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:21.580
The Disas Army may have been defeated,

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.280
but these guys were once special forces.

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:25.920
They know their job, gi.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.920
This is our Magical Operations Response Group,

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.570
a.k.a. MORG.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.730
Cage here is Team 1's captain.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:35.460
I'm Cage.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:39.080
I'm honored to get to work with such legends.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.690
Glad to have you.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:46.170
The Foreign Affairs Minister and America's
ambassador to Japan are also attending, right?

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:50.130
As are the Magical Security Council
 and WTO staff.

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:52.340
VIPs as far as the eye can see, huh?

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.560
This is an important job, then.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:58.280
There's still time before the conference.

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:00.930
The bureaucrats are on the ground
doing some last minute preparations.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:04.400
M Squad and MORG are to undergo
a final briefing in the shelter.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:10.830
So what about us?

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:15.370
Supposedly, they want to talk to the Magical 
Girls in private before the conference.

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:19.160
It was a personal request
from General Tabira.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.810
That's probably bad news.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:44.440
General Tabira...

00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:48.520
It's been a long time, Asuka.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:52.480
And you too, Kurumi, Tamara, and Mia.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:57.020
I heard you didn't want to fight anymore!

00:09:53.650 --> 00:10:00.620
<b>Rub
Rub</b>

00:09:53.650 --> 00:10:00.620
<b>Rub
Rub</b>

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:58.350
You poor thing!

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.620
Tell Mommy all about it!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:06.580
<b>Rub Rub Rub</b>

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:03.990
Give Mommy Tabira a big hug and a kiss!

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:06.580
Yeah, that's as rough as ever.

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:09.560
Is that General Tabira?

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:10.830
That's right.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:13.160
You never really got to talk to her.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.260
General Tabira is one of the top
 generals serving Meripiko,

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.140
one of the core countries of the 
Spirit World Treaty Organization.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:24.760
Her one flaw is her excessive
expressions of love for the Magical Girls.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.180
Knock it off!

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.810
You're in a bad mood, huh, Asuka?

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:32.100
Want to play with my boobs?

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:33.150
Hell no!

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:35.570
Mia, you always preferred
my ass, didn't you?

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.150
Don't make shit up!

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.120
Finish your job and go home!

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.070
Oh no...

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:47.890
And I was looking forward
to seeing you today.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:52.090
I brought you presents, too.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.210
Kataru!

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:55.080
Of course, taru.

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:56.170
What is it?

00:10:56.860 --> 00:11:01.640
New Magical Girl outfits that
will enhance your power.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.090
I think you'll look great in it!

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:08.060
Slingshot swimsuit maid outfits!

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.580
I've heard about your situation.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:18.360
Now you'll have no trouble with
the modified Disas, or even new Disas!

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.680
How could you do that?

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.530
Mouse-types are so lame, ru.

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:27.960
Tamara, don't set it on fire!

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:28.000
How come somebody like that
gets to be with a Magical Girl, taru?

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:33.620
Looks like you want to taste the punch
of a fairy who survived the great war, chu!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.590
Cat-types and mouse-types don't get along.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.010
Now, let's get down to business.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:47.390
Oh dear.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.150
This one's for real.

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:54.520
A powerful, newly-developed magical item.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.710
You won't be able to use it right now,

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:04.580
but it has the power to enhance your
magical abilities several times over.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.090
And you're giving it to us?

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:08.700
Yes.

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:32.090
Establishing sensory link between
forward observation, fire control,

00:12:32.090 --> 00:12:35.560
and the Cenobite-class.

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:39.380
They're synchronized
down to the millisecond, gi.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:43.070
Decide on a base fire Disas and begin aiming.

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:45.060
If you miss at this range,

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:46.990
you're demoted to Gremlin-class.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:53.390
Telepathically transmitting indirect
fire grid and artillery data link

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:57.340
to all support Disas in the units
participating in the attack.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:58.960
Begin the mission.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.170
Do it as planned.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.590
<b>JASDF Naha Base</b>

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.070
Forward observation reports a hit.

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:13.350
Adjust for error and fire for effect, gi.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.290
Roger.

00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:16.600
All Cenobite-classes, open fire.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.150
<b>JGSDF Naha Garrison</b>

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:27.450
An old soldier once said that

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:31.280
the field of battle is sown
by artillery and reaped by infantry.

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:33.120
Smart!

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.040
Enemy force is continuing their indirect fire.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.700
We are currently on the fifth
round of bombardment.

00:13:38.940 --> 00:13:42.210
Naha Garrison's administration office
and barracks have suffered heavy damage.

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.440
Our units on standby have
taken multiple casualties.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:46.970
We're getting the full numbers now.

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:49.800
You're the Special Operations Group
 and Magical Girls, right?

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.420
There's no time for long introductions.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:53.560
<b>15th Brigade Commander
Major General Horibe Masao</b>

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:53.550
I'll get right to the point.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.770
<b>Brigade Vice-Commander and Naha Garrison Commander
Colonel Higa Kojiro</b>

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:57.980
The enemy forces greatly
exceed our expectations.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:57.980
<b>Staff Officer 
Colonel Miyama Tsuneo</b>

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.210
This isn't a security mission.

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:01.350
This is a war.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:03.520
Humanity's ability to fight magical wars

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:05.880
is dependent on our alliance
with the Spirit World.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:09.950
And the Naha Garrison Bridge
is what makes that alliance possible.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:14.190
That makes this the most
important spot on Earth.

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:16.910
We must protect it at all costs.

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:20.500
We want the help of you Magical Girls.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.370
Yes, sir!

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:25.100
All Cenobite-classes have
expended their magic.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:28.130
Returning them to compressed
form until recovery.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:33.710
3rd Battalion, begin attack.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:34.790
1st Battalion,

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:36.850
split into four companies,

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:39.780
surround Naha Garrison,
and attack it from both flanks.

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:40.850
Kilgy!

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:46.780
<b>Naha City</b>

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.110
<b>I thought I heard a loud noise, so I went to look...</b>

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.110
<b>There was a loud boom from the Naha Garrison. Not good.</b>

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:50.110
<b>I can see smoke from here. Was there an accident? How scary.</b>

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:54.980
It's so cold!

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:56.860
That's not quite right.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:57.950
What isn't?

00:14:57.950 --> 00:15:00.800
You're a teenage girl eating ice cream.

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.950
You need to make it seem
dirtier when you lick it!

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:07.660
I'll toss you into the ocean.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:18.350
Where's the Naha Base 9th Air Wing?

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:21.730
An enemy artillery strike
hit their alert hangar.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.450
We're still waiting
for a full damage report,

00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:26.970
but right now we've received word
that the F-15s are unable to scramble.

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:29.330
And the U.S. military bases?

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:35.280
The enemy attacks were concentrated on
the JASDF Naha Base and JGSDF Naha Garrison.

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:38.880
No attacks on the U.S. military bases
 in Okinawa were detected.

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:39.740
What?

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:42.700
The enemy is trying to avoid
involving the US military.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:45.100
What about the Japan-U.S. Security Treaty?

00:15:45.100 --> 00:15:49.030
Without a single attack on a U.S. base...

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:52.090
We can't expect them
to send in the Marines, huh?

00:15:55.270 --> 00:15:57.610
The Cabinet has just made its decision.

00:15:57.610 --> 00:15:59.720
In light of extenuating circumstances,

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:03.200
permission to counterattack is granted under
the Response to Magic-Related Incidents Act.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:05.230
What kind of firepower did it authorize?

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:06.620
All we've got.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:09.130
The Minister of Defense
will take responsibility.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:10.140
Roger.

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:11.400
What's the enemy doing?

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:14.610
Disas have appeared in Naha City.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:17.040
We've confirmed the presence
of modified Halloween-class.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:22.250
The Okinawa Prefectural Police have engaged
the enemy and are evacuating civilians, but...

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:28.970
That's hopeless!

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:32.800
The Okinawa Prefectural Police
can't fight a Halloween-class!

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:34.780
What about the 15th Brigade?

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:37.700
We took some damage in that bombardment,
 but it's minor.

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:42.270
The 15th Brigade will be our primary
force as we engage the enemy.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:45.370
We brought an Osprey
for the security mission.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:47.350
I read that report.

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:48.810
We'll be counting on you.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:53.820
M Squad and the U.S. MORG
are our best weapons against the Disas.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:56.110
Let's work together to get through this.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:56.650
Of course.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:00.900
Our issue is the enemy in Naha City.

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:03.870
The enemy is clearly after our bridge.

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:07.900
They're attacking the police
and civilians to lure us away.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:10.020
Of course, I know that.

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:12.700
But if we don't stop them, 
they'll burn Naha to the ground!

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:15.840
<b>Tomorrow's free time
I'll buy you something in the city and
 bring it back
Let's hang out again when I get home</b>

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.160
I'll go.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.440
I can't allow that.

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:24.320
Rapture excels at close-range combat,

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:26.560
and is the core of our defense of the base.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.140
We can't send you there.

00:17:29.410 --> 00:17:31.960
Well, Iizuka-san's right.

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:35.820
So I'll go.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:41.730
Magical Girls have extrajudicial
authorization to fight Disas.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.050
I don't know how many decoys they brought,

00:17:45.050 --> 00:17:46.660
but I'll get rid of them all.

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:49.150
But even if they're just decoys,

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.880
they have Halloween-classes!

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:52.910
You can't go alone!

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:57.160
You're so kind, Kurumi.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.720
Just like that old guy over there said,

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:04.190
the enemy is clearly after the 6th Naha.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:07.810
Which means we can't move any
of our defensive forces from the base.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:11.530
But if you need to deal with those decoys,

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:14.630
you need to send somebody who can deal

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:18.780
with a Halloween-class on their own, right?

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:20.240
Mia?

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:22.450
Then it's settled.

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:25.840
We've established a defensive
perimeter in a circle

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:28.090
around the camouflaged shelter.

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:31.090
The 15th Brigade, M Squad,

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:33.810
and the U.S.'s MORG will be deployed here.

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:35.490
I'll go there, too.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:37.320
Tamara?

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:38.970
If there are a lot of enemies,

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:40.680
then you need me.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:44.890
Fighting in a circular defensive
perimeter is what I'm best at.

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:50.650
And as for any Disas that make it
through the defenses to the basement...

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:54.270
Kurumi and I will handle them?

00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:57.870
What do you think, Commander Horibe?

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:02.270
You have the most experience with
magical combat of anybody here.

00:19:02.270 --> 00:19:03.860
Let's go with your plan.

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:05.490
And General Tabira.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:06.220
Yes?

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:08.760
Please retreat to the Spirit World.

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.080
I refuse!

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:12.260
Of course,

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:14.210
I'll fight with all of you.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.770
I'm afraid I can't allow that.

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.040
Iizuka!

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:19.780
If anything happens to you,

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:22.610
it's a loss to all humanity.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:26.440
This isn't an issue of anyone's
personal feelings.

00:19:26.440 --> 00:19:29.440
It's a critical matter for both worlds.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:30.850
Well, yes, but...

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.490
General!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.260
Mia...

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.230
Please...

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:45.210
Don't die.

00:19:47.050 --> 00:19:48.560
Of course I won't.

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:51.000
Let me go.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:52.740
I'm blushing.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.670
When I heard M Squad
was getting one of these,

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.640
I thought it was a little too much...

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:05.220
But it's about to be useful already.

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:14.810
Multiple enemy Disas
are approaching the main gate!

00:20:15.390 --> 00:20:17.230
We know that bullets
work on Gremlin-classes,

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:22.650
and grenades and MANPATS
are effective against Voorhees-classes!

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.000
Most Disas are vulnerable
to normal arms fire,

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.910
if it's concentrated enough!

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.330
<b>JSDF Naha Garrison: Vicinity of the Front Gate</b>

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:34.080
These 12.7mm magical
rounds are rare as hell!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.170
They're worth more than your
balls are, so aim carefully!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.840
<b>Front Gate: East Side, Roof
US Military Magical Operations Response Group (MORG)
Roof Squad</b>

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:40.210
The enemy's strategic objective is

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.510
to sever the link between
Earth and the Spirit World!

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:45.970
Pay them back for what
they did in the great war!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:49.230
Our JTF's primary units have engaged
the enemy near the front gate!

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:52.610
Enemy air units approaching
from the Naha naval base side!

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.670
Shit!

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.300
Volshebnyy Ognemet!

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.060
I'm sorry this happened.

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:12.230
The trade negotiations
can take place again soon.

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:13.330
Of course.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.630
This isn't the Japanese government's fault.

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:18.790
Kataru...

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:19.890
Right, taru!

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:21.680
Taru.

00:21:23.690 --> 00:21:25.340
The bridge has shut down!

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:26.300
What?

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:29.760
There are signs of a Dimensional 
Explosive having been used, taru!

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:31.790
A Dimensional Explosive?

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:34.100
A type of magical bomb that destroys

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:36.220
the methods used to move
between worlds, chu!

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:40.560
If the enemy used a
Dimensional Explosive now, then...

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:43.570
They're not after the 6th Naha.

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:45.860
They're after General Tabira!

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:50.540
So they want her no matter
what it takes, huh?

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:53.360
How long before the bridge
comes back online?

00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:57.500
The enemy appears to have only
used one relatively small bomb.

00:21:57.500 --> 00:21:58.530
But...

00:21:58.530 --> 00:22:01.380
It'll take at least 48 hours!

00:22:01.940 --> 00:22:03.080
Two days...

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:09.660
We just need to protect General Tabira, right?

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:18.140
Let's go join them, Chisato.

00:22:19.340 --> 00:22:20.190
Yeah.

00:23:57.550 --> 00:24:00.820
Asuka, Kurumi, Mia, and Tamara
are all fighting in separate locations!

00:24:00.820 --> 00:24:03.290
Even if normal weapons don't work
very well against their enemy,

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:06.300
the soldiers do their best
for the Magical Girls!

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:08.250
Next time: "Each of Their Deadly Battles."

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:09.840
<b>Each of Their Deadly Battles</b>

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:11.540
With your Magical Karambit,
rip the bad guys to pieces, chu!
